1
00:00:12,012 --> 00:00:15,473
<i>‎We'd spent so long preparing
‎and practicing for the cultural festival,</i>

2
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:18,767
<i>‎and then it was over before we knew it.</i>

3
00:00:18,768 --> 00:00:20,894
‎Did you take that carpet home?

4
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:22,730
‎I can't take it home.

5
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:24,691
‎-<i>‎And the following day...</i>
‎-What a waste.

6
00:00:29,279 --> 00:00:32,699
{\an8}‎MOMOKA - TODAY
‎IT'S BEEN A WHILE

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,702
‎Sorry to reach out so suddenly.

8
00:00:36,369 --> 00:00:38,705
‎I've been meaning to talk to you, Koyun.

9
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,459
‎Yeah. Same here.

10
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,296
‎You go first.

11
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,548
‎I'll be frank.

12
00:00:49,549 --> 00:00:52,093
‎I want you to stay away from Minato.

13
00:02:26,604 --> 00:02:30,942
‎EPISODE 21
‎MISUNDERSTANDINGS

14
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:36,447
<i>‎I've always known
‎I'm a walking contradiction.</i>

15
00:02:37,615 --> 00:02:40,409
<i>‎I keep telling myself she's not a threat,</i>

16
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:43,705
<i>‎and yet I can't stand her presence.</i>

17
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:46,332
<i>‎I hate her.</i>

18
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:49,836
<i>‎I did ask. So many times.</i>

19
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,838
<i>‎If she really did like Minato,</i>

20
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:55,091
<i>‎she should have held onto him
‎and never let him go.</i>

21
00:02:56,301 --> 00:02:58,803
<i>‎It's rude to get close to him now.</i>

22
00:02:59,304 --> 00:03:00,763
‎-<i>‎It's nasty--</i>
‎-All right.

23
00:03:02,307 --> 00:03:04,017
{\an8}‎I'll stay away from Amamiya.

24
00:03:04,559 --> 00:03:05,642
‎MATSURI - ONDO NO MASTER

25
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:10,398
<i>‎You mean you don't like us
‎hanging out even as a group, right?</i>

26
00:03:11,232 --> 00:03:14,736
‎Or do you want me
‎to cut ties with him completely?

27
00:03:15,695 --> 00:03:17,488
‎Well, I...

28
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:21,617
‎We'll still have to talk,
‎because we're in the same class,

29
00:03:21,618 --> 00:03:23,286
‎so that could be difficult.

30
00:03:24,037 --> 00:03:26,330
‎I wouldn't want to be rude, after all.

31
00:03:26,331 --> 00:03:31,461
‎Though I guess whether that's rude or not
‎depends on you and Amamiya.

32
00:03:32,086 --> 00:03:34,338
<i>‎It depends on Minato?</i>

33
00:03:34,339 --> 00:03:39,260
<i>‎Are you saying that because
‎you're so sure he'd choose you instead?</i>

34
00:03:39,969 --> 00:03:41,095
<i>‎What is with this girl?</i>

35
00:03:41,596 --> 00:03:43,765
<i>‎She's acting like this is no big deal.</i>

36
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,517
<i>‎I'm his girlfriend.</i>

37
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:48,770
<i>‎I'm the one in her way.</i>

38
00:03:50,813 --> 00:03:53,775
‎Really?
‎You're okay with it just like that?

39
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:57,695
‎I know you've always denied it,

40
00:03:58,529 --> 00:04:00,281
‎but you like Minato, don't you?

41
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:06,246
‎Whether I like him or not
‎has nothing to do with your relationship.

42
00:04:07,038 --> 00:04:08,790
‎He's going out with you.

43
00:04:09,499 --> 00:04:11,084
‎He chose you.

44
00:04:12,877 --> 00:04:16,005
‎I'm sorry if I've done anything
‎to give you the wrong impression,

45
00:04:16,589 --> 00:04:21,051
{\an8}‎but ever since you two started dating,

46
00:04:21,052 --> 00:04:24,806
{\an8}‎he's only ever treated me as a friend.

47
00:04:25,473 --> 00:04:28,559
‎I believe he's genuinely in this for you.

48
00:04:29,769 --> 00:04:33,147
<i>‎Amamiya and I are just friends.</i>

49
00:04:34,315 --> 00:04:36,733
‎If you still don't trust me,

50
00:04:36,734 --> 00:04:40,154
‎I'll stay away from him
‎for as long as you want me to.

51
00:04:41,614 --> 00:04:44,784
{\an8}‎Please have faith in Amamiya.

52
00:04:47,161 --> 00:04:48,663
<i>‎Why?</i>

53
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:52,541
{\an8}‎I asked if you like him,
‎and you didn't deny it.

54
00:04:52,542 --> 00:04:54,001
{\an8}‎Isn't that an answer in itself?

55
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:55,252
‎SHOW SOMETHING, ANYTHING

56
00:04:55,253 --> 00:04:56,336
‎I CAN TELL
‎YOU'RE UNHAPPY ABOUT THIS

57
00:04:56,337 --> 00:04:58,755
<i>‎Why am I the one being admonished here?</i>

58
00:04:58,756 --> 00:05:00,132
‎GOODY-TWO-SHOES
‎ACTING LIKE SHE'S ABOVE IT ALL

59
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,216
‎COMING UP WITH
‎ALL SORTS OF THEORIES

60
00:05:01,217 --> 00:05:02,759
<i>‎It's almost as if</i>

61
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,345
<i>‎I'm the one at fault.</i>

62
00:05:06,264 --> 00:05:08,891
<i>‎When I'm the one who came
‎to end things once and for all.</i>

63
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:14,313
‎I'm glad you're being
‎reasonable about this.

64
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:17,567
‎You have the common sense to give up
‎on your man because he has a girlfriend.

65
00:05:18,151 --> 00:05:20,319
‎I mean, sure, we're dating,

66
00:05:20,320 --> 00:05:23,071
‎but there's no contract stating
‎we're getting married or anything.

67
00:05:23,072 --> 00:05:24,907
‎It's all just verbal agreement, right?

68
00:05:25,408 --> 00:05:26,491
‎I'M JUST THE PERSON HE'S DATING

69
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:30,246
<i>‎I worry when the two of you are together.</i>

70
00:05:30,913 --> 00:05:32,998
‎Because if it were me,

71
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:36,085
‎I'd keep trying,
‎even if he had a girlfriend.

72
00:05:36,669 --> 00:05:37,836
‎WHAT MAKES ME SO WORRIED...

73
00:05:37,837 --> 00:05:40,590
<i>‎I wouldn't give up just like that.</i>

74
00:05:41,799 --> 00:05:45,177
<i>‎I don't want someone as apathetic as her...</i>

75
00:05:45,178 --> 00:05:46,970
‎I DEFINITELY

76
00:05:46,971 --> 00:05:48,055
‎LOVE HIM MORE

77
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:49,599
<i>‎...to steal him from me.</i>

78
00:05:54,896 --> 00:05:56,647
‎What do you mean by "keep trying"?

79
00:05:57,982 --> 00:06:01,235
‎I concede that things are as they are
‎because you put in the effort.

80
00:06:02,070 --> 00:06:06,448
‎But to "keep trying"
‎even when they like someone else,

81
00:06:06,449 --> 00:06:07,867
‎that's got to be selfish, right?

82
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:13,163
‎I can at least assure you that I won't
‎force my feelings onto him like that.

83
00:06:13,164 --> 00:06:17,376
<i>‎You keep holding back for others,
‎and you'll just lose out in life.</i>

84
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:19,003
‎Well,

85
00:06:19,587 --> 00:06:22,006
‎I guess it doesn't matter what I think.

86
00:06:23,299 --> 00:06:27,136
‎It's not like we need
‎to understand each other.

87
00:06:28,221 --> 00:06:29,554
<i>‎Hostility.</i>

88
00:06:29,555 --> 00:06:34,559
{\an8}‎You know, you associate with others
‎with no hesitation at all.

89
00:06:34,560 --> 00:06:38,355
{\an8}‎You grow your social networks
‎for your own goals.

90
00:06:38,356 --> 00:06:40,565
{\an8}‎You're always so sure of yourself.

91
00:06:40,566 --> 00:06:42,734
<i>‎Such malice behind those words.</i>

92
00:06:42,735 --> 00:06:44,194
<i>‎Is she trying to tell me off?</i>

93
00:06:44,195 --> 00:06:45,905
‎I mean it when I say this...

94
00:06:46,781 --> 00:06:48,908
{\an8}‎I've always envied you.

95
00:06:50,159 --> 00:06:51,326
{\an8}‎What?

96
00:06:51,327 --> 00:06:53,745
‎You take action,
‎and you can make your own choices.

97
00:06:53,746 --> 00:06:56,124
‎You must have great self-confidence.

98
00:06:56,791 --> 00:06:58,417
‎You're the complete opposite to me.

99
00:06:59,502 --> 00:07:02,629
{\an8}‎I've always envied you, Momoka.

100
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:05,508
{\an8}‎You envy me?

101
00:07:06,008 --> 00:07:08,302
‎I really, truly do envy you,

102
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:12,223
‎but I still can't bring myself
‎to behave the way you do.

103
00:07:13,057 --> 00:07:14,599
‎Why not?

104
00:07:14,600 --> 00:07:17,186
‎I think when you deal with people,

105
00:07:18,312 --> 00:07:20,313
{\an8}‎you must draw a clear line

106
00:07:20,314 --> 00:07:23,109
{\an8}‎between those you want to get to know
‎and those you don't care about.

107
00:07:24,026 --> 00:07:25,570
‎Well, of course.

108
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:29,240
‎It's tiring having to treat
‎everyone exactly the same.

109
00:07:30,908 --> 00:07:32,743
‎I do get that.

110
00:07:33,453 --> 00:07:34,579
‎But...

111
00:07:35,621 --> 00:07:40,084
‎Momoka's been hanging out with you
‎a lot recently, hasn't she?

112
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:42,879
‎When she used to hang out with me.

113
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:46,424
‎You do know why, right?

114
00:07:48,009 --> 00:07:50,094
{\an8}‎You can't treat people
‎based on how useful they are.

115
00:07:50,761 --> 00:07:53,222
{\an8}‎You can't treat people like pawns.

116
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:55,600
{\an8}‎Where did all this come from?

117
00:07:56,267 --> 00:08:00,062
{\an8}‎What could I have possibly done
‎to make you say these things?

118
00:08:00,980 --> 00:08:02,314
{\an8}‎Nothing.

119
00:08:02,315 --> 00:08:04,358
{\an8}‎You don't have to feel anything for me.

120
00:08:05,610 --> 00:08:10,865
<i>‎But the people you don't care about,
‎the ones you treat as pawns,</i>

121
00:08:11,657 --> 00:08:15,495
<i>‎they have worries, and they can feel hurt.</i>

122
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:17,914
<i>‎They're still human, like you.</i>

123
00:08:19,290 --> 00:08:21,000
‎You can try and hide it,

124
00:08:21,667 --> 00:08:24,253
‎but people can tell
‎when they're being used.

125
00:08:24,754 --> 00:08:26,005
‎It's not a nice feeling.

126
00:08:26,756 --> 00:08:28,256
{\an8}‎It's one thing to not care,

127
00:08:28,257 --> 00:08:30,218
{\an8}‎but another to treat people
‎however you want.

128
00:08:30,843 --> 00:08:32,261
{\an8}‎That is all

129
00:08:33,471 --> 00:08:35,389
{\an8}‎I wanted to tell you today.

130
00:08:42,855 --> 00:08:44,064
‎HEH

131
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,608
‎Guess you really hate me, huh?

132
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:50,111
‎Well, I'm used to girls not liking me.

133
00:08:50,112 --> 00:08:51,239
‎No.

134
00:08:51,864 --> 00:08:54,367
‎I don't hate you.

135
00:08:54,867 --> 00:09:00,206
‎I mean, I barely know you,
‎so how could I hate you?

136
00:09:01,123 --> 00:09:02,458
‎And the same goes for you.

137
00:09:03,501 --> 00:09:09,006
‎It's just that I don't agree
‎with some of your actions.

138
00:09:10,383 --> 00:09:11,466
‎SMILE

139
00:09:11,467 --> 00:09:12,802
‎Thanks for the heads up.

140
00:09:13,386 --> 00:09:19,308
‎But surely we're the ones who need to act
‎to make sure we are happy in life, right?

141
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:22,519
‎They say to be equally kind to everyone.

142
00:09:22,520 --> 00:09:25,272
‎They say to be considerate of others.

143
00:09:25,273 --> 00:09:27,942
‎I don't think I can do that.

144
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:31,112
‎Because I'm selfish.

145
00:09:33,906 --> 00:09:35,950
{\an8}‎I can't do it either.

146
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:40,705
‎But if all you ever do is act
‎in your own self-interests,

147
00:09:41,455 --> 00:09:44,083
‎you'll end up focusing on
‎all the parts where you're lacking.

148
00:09:45,001 --> 00:09:47,503
‎In the end, it'll only leave you unhappy.

149
00:09:50,006 --> 00:09:52,800
‎Was that referring to yourself?

150
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:55,136
‎Or was that addressed to me?

151
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:57,679
{\an8}‎Both.

152
00:09:57,680 --> 00:10:00,349
{\an8}‎Which is why all I want for the two of you

153
00:10:00,850 --> 00:10:03,686
{\an8}‎is for you to be happy
‎in your relationship.

154
00:10:05,605 --> 00:10:06,606
‎So,

155
00:10:07,273 --> 00:10:08,691
{\an8}‎I'll keep my distance.

156
00:10:09,692 --> 00:10:10,943
‎Will that be okay?

157
00:10:13,613 --> 00:10:14,614
{\an8}‎Yes.

158
00:10:18,242 --> 00:10:19,744
<i>‎I hate her.</i>

159
00:10:21,245 --> 00:10:25,624
<i>‎I hate her, so everything she does,
‎her very existence,</i>

160
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:27,877
<i>‎irritates me to no end.</i>

161
00:10:29,545 --> 00:10:36,010
<i>‎I'd rather she just come out
‎and say she hates my guts.</i>

162
00:10:37,011 --> 00:10:41,349
<i>‎If she would just be the enemy,
‎then I could fight against her in my mind.</i>

163
00:10:42,391 --> 00:10:44,226
<i>‎Then I would be justified.</i>

164
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:47,688
<i>‎I won just now.</i>

165
00:10:48,689 --> 00:10:50,733
<i>‎So why do I feel so empty?</i>

166
00:10:53,611 --> 00:10:55,237
‎And I kept saying so.

167
00:10:56,489 --> 00:10:58,574
‎So then Hayato...

168
00:10:59,325 --> 00:11:01,243
‎SULLEN

169
00:11:02,036 --> 00:11:03,037
‎Momoka?

170
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:07,083
‎What's wrong?

171
00:11:12,004 --> 00:11:13,255
‎Minato.

172
00:11:14,048 --> 00:11:15,341
‎Do you even like me?

173
00:11:18,677 --> 00:11:20,178
{\an8}‎Yeah. I like you.

174
00:11:20,179 --> 00:11:21,222
{\an8}‎What do you like about me?

175
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:25,183
{\an8}‎I like that you're confident
‎and feisty... and you're clever.

176
00:11:25,184 --> 00:11:28,521
{\an8}‎Aren't those sort of backhanded
‎compliments to give to a girl?

177
00:11:29,313 --> 00:11:30,980
‎You make me sound calculating.

178
00:11:30,981 --> 00:11:31,982
{\an8}‎I MEAN, I AM, BUT...

179
00:11:33,484 --> 00:11:34,819
‎But it's good to be cautious.

180
00:11:36,695 --> 00:11:37,696
‎Well...

181
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:40,783
‎Who do you like more? Me, or Koyun?

182
00:11:41,575 --> 00:11:43,953
{\an8}‎Why do you ask? Koyun's my friend.

183
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:46,621
{\an8}‎She's like Miki or Yota.

184
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:48,416
‎It's a different kind of "like."

185
00:11:48,999 --> 00:11:52,837
{\an8}‎But what if Koyun came to you
‎right now and said she liked you?

186
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:56,589
{\an8}‎You'd choose her, right?

187
00:11:56,590 --> 00:11:58,174
{\an8}‎I wouldn't.

188
00:11:58,175 --> 00:12:00,052
{\an8}‎Because I'm going out with you.

189
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,058
<i>‎Because we're going out?</i>

190
00:12:06,934 --> 00:12:09,061
<i>‎What am I still doing wrong here?</i>

191
00:12:09,854 --> 00:12:11,981
<i>‎I feel like I'm doing everything right,</i>

192
00:12:13,190 --> 00:12:15,358
<i>‎but I'm still going down this same path.</i>

193
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:16,569
‎GO AHEAD
‎THAT'S FINE

194
00:12:17,194 --> 00:12:18,863
<i>‎Why is she still worried?</i>

195
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,615
{\an8}‎I'm sorry to make you worry.

196
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:24,201
‎What can I do to make it better?

197
00:12:24,994 --> 00:12:27,413
‎What do you want me to do?

198
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:31,709
‎Can you not be so logical about this!

199
00:12:32,293 --> 00:12:33,793
{\an8}‎We're talking about feelings here.

200
00:12:33,794 --> 00:12:35,588
{\an8}‎It's about what feelings you prioritize.

201
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:42,303
‎Okay, I want you to stay away from Koyun.

202
00:12:42,803 --> 00:12:46,222
‎You say you're just friends,
‎but I don't like how close you two are.

203
00:12:46,223 --> 00:12:48,517
‎I hate how well you get along!

204
00:12:52,480 --> 00:12:53,481
‎All right.

205
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:57,443
‎But how much do I need
‎to stay away from her?

206
00:12:58,277 --> 00:13:01,280
‎You mean you don't like us
‎hanging out as friends, right?

207
00:13:01,822 --> 00:13:04,574
‎Or do you want me
‎to cut ties with her completely?

208
00:13:04,575 --> 00:13:08,286
{\an8}‎We'll still have to talk,
‎because we're in the same class,

209
00:13:08,287 --> 00:13:10,038
{\an8}‎so that could be difficult.

210
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:12,249
{\an8}‎DÉJÀ VU...

211
00:13:13,292 --> 00:13:15,251
‎Oh, my gosh!

212
00:13:15,252 --> 00:13:17,755
‎-Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh! Oh, my gosh!
‎-What's wrong?

213
00:13:23,761 --> 00:13:25,720
‎Dad says he doesn't need dinner.

214
00:13:25,721 --> 00:13:27,556
‎He could have said so sooner.

215
00:13:28,933 --> 00:13:31,644
‎Minato. Will you eat it for me?

216
00:13:38,984 --> 00:13:40,277
‎I can't eat all this.

217
00:13:41,529 --> 00:13:43,781
‎Normally you'd wolf it down.

218
00:13:44,823 --> 00:13:47,660
<i>‎Something's wrong...</i>

219
00:13:53,332 --> 00:13:54,416
<i>‎I can't sleep.</i>

220
00:13:57,461 --> 00:14:00,214
<i>‎Dating is hard.</i>

221
00:14:02,091 --> 00:14:04,467
{\an8}<i>‎It's about what feelings you prioritize.</i>

222
00:14:04,468 --> 00:14:07,220
<i>‎Thank you for being my friend.</i>

223
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:09,889
{\an8}<i>‎I hope one day,
‎you fall in love with someone...</i>

224
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:13,434
<i>‎Well, I'd love to see you in love someday.</i>

225
00:14:13,435 --> 00:14:14,436
<i>‎But how do you feel?</i>

226
00:14:23,821 --> 00:14:26,907
<i>‎How do I fall asleep again?</i>

227
00:14:29,994 --> 00:14:31,077
‎ZONKED

228
00:14:31,078 --> 00:14:33,247
<i>‎I don't think I slept at all.</i>

229
00:14:33,831 --> 00:14:37,293
‎Minato. You've been grinding
‎your teeth at night lately.

230
00:14:38,002 --> 00:14:40,670
‎Are you maybe stressed?

231
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:41,672
‎Me?

232
00:14:43,299 --> 00:14:46,009
‎I guess not.
‎Our little unbothered, youngest child.

233
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,177
‎Yeah.

234
00:14:47,928 --> 00:14:51,682
<i>‎I have been feeling a little off lately.</i>

235
00:14:52,349 --> 00:14:54,435
<i>‎And my head feels really uncomfortable...</i>

236
00:14:56,270 --> 00:14:58,229
{\an8}‎Ouch...

237
00:14:58,230 --> 00:15:00,523
{\an8}‎-What's wrong?
‎-I can't...

238
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:02,275
‎Minato?

239
00:15:02,276 --> 00:15:03,819
‎It hurts...

240
00:15:05,779 --> 00:15:07,322
‎Are you all right, Minato?

241
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:08,699
‎Hey!

242
00:15:09,742 --> 00:15:11,076
{\an8}‎It's stress.

243
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:13,411
{\an8}‎Stress?

244
00:15:13,412 --> 00:15:16,874
‎Yes. It appears differently for everyone.

245
00:15:17,416 --> 00:15:22,630
‎It can sometimes build up slowly over time
‎from the little things you barely notice.

246
00:15:24,006 --> 00:15:27,383
‎Either way,
‎your mind's exhausted right now.

247
00:15:27,384 --> 00:15:29,719
‎I'll give you some meds,
‎and we'll keep an eye on it.

248
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:34,474
‎If it doesn't get better,
‎you could consider a psychosomatic clinic.

249
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:36,143
<i>‎Psychosomatic clinic?</i>

250
00:15:36,769 --> 00:15:39,687
{\an8}‎It's a good thing I don't have college
‎until the afternoon today.

251
00:15:39,688 --> 00:15:41,023
{\an8}‎Yeah.

252
00:15:41,607 --> 00:15:44,526
‎You need to take
‎better care of yourself, Minato.

253
00:15:45,027 --> 00:15:46,028
‎Yeah.

254
00:15:47,363 --> 00:15:49,615
<i>‎I'm stressed? Over what?</i>

255
00:15:50,616 --> 00:15:53,535
‎Oops, the hand brake was still on.

256
00:15:59,416 --> 00:16:03,045
{\an8}‎We're home, but now I have to park.
‎I can do this, right?

257
00:16:03,671 --> 00:16:05,965
‎Minato. You go on inside first.

258
00:16:06,548 --> 00:16:07,549
‎Okay.

259
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:13,180
{\an8}<i>‎What? The door's not locked?</i>

260
00:16:13,806 --> 00:16:14,932
<i>‎Why not?</i>

261
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,393
{\an8}‎-What?
‎-Whoa!

262
00:16:19,979 --> 00:16:21,772
‎Oh, it's just Minato.

263
00:16:23,065 --> 00:16:24,441
{\an8}‎Kaito!

264
00:16:28,529 --> 00:16:29,612
‎Sorry to startle you.

265
00:16:29,613 --> 00:16:33,492
‎Could you not sneak in
‎like some kind of burglar?

266
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:36,369
‎How rude. This used to be my home too.

267
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:40,915
‎You did say "Whoa" when I saw you though.

268
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,543
{\an8}‎Yeah, about that...

269
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:45,044
{\an8}‎I'm here for the seal.

270
00:16:45,045 --> 00:16:46,462
{\an8}‎You are a burglar!

271
00:16:46,463 --> 00:16:49,800
‎It's what I used to open my bank account
‎when I was still living here.

272
00:16:50,843 --> 00:16:52,260
‎Whatever.

273
00:16:52,261 --> 00:16:55,680
‎I'm going to college.
‎You do whatever you like.

274
00:16:55,681 --> 00:16:56,807
{\an8}‎Buh-bye.

275
00:16:57,808 --> 00:17:01,394
{\an8}‎And Minato's not feeling well today,
‎so don't bother him for too long.

276
00:17:01,395 --> 00:17:03,312
‎What? He's unwell?

277
00:17:03,313 --> 00:17:05,024
‎We just got back from the doctor's office.

278
00:17:05,566 --> 00:17:07,900
‎But I'm feeling okay now.

279
00:17:07,901 --> 00:17:08,902
{\an8}‎Bye.

280
00:17:12,281 --> 00:17:13,824
{\an8}‎-See you.
‎-Yep.

281
00:17:16,535 --> 00:17:18,536
‎It's weird seeing you two not fight.

282
00:17:18,537 --> 00:17:19,788
‎How old do you think I am?

283
00:17:20,914 --> 00:17:23,541
{\an8}‎But you, Minato. You're not feeling well?

284
00:17:23,542 --> 00:17:25,835
‎No, I'm fine.

285
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:28,672
‎I think I'm just tired.

286
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:32,759
{\an8}‎The doctor said something about
‎not letting stress build up too much.

287
00:17:32,760 --> 00:17:34,678
{\an8}‎I see...

288
00:17:35,512 --> 00:17:39,266
‎Well, you are you,
‎so it's no wonder you get stressed.

289
00:17:40,601 --> 00:17:41,602
‎Listen, Minato.

290
00:17:42,603 --> 00:17:46,857
{\an8}‎You tend to go with the flow
‎and then keep things inside.

291
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:51,987
{\an8}‎You stifle what you want to say
‎and keep everything bottled up.

292
00:17:52,571 --> 00:17:54,030
{\an8}‎You always have.

293
00:17:54,031 --> 00:17:55,157
{\an8}‎Surely, I...

294
00:17:55,783 --> 00:17:56,784
‎I'm sorry.

295
00:17:57,409 --> 00:18:02,247
‎It's because you saw me
‎always getting chewed out by Mom and Dad.

296
00:18:02,748 --> 00:18:04,833
‎I was pretty much the example
‎of what not to do.

297
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:09,128
<i>‎You saw me get shunned
‎for doing as I pleased,</i>

298
00:18:09,129 --> 00:18:10,839
<i>‎so it's no wonder you turned out this way.</i>

299
00:18:11,965 --> 00:18:15,094
<i>‎You were the only one
‎in this house who had my back,</i>

300
00:18:15,677 --> 00:18:17,513
‎and that put you in a tough position.

301
00:18:18,680 --> 00:18:22,601
‎I put you through that,
‎and for that, I'm sorry.

302
00:18:23,811 --> 00:18:25,395
{\an8}‎What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

303
00:18:26,814 --> 00:18:30,067
{\an8}‎You were never one to analyze people.

304
00:18:30,567 --> 00:18:31,610
{\an8}‎Say what?

305
00:18:32,319 --> 00:18:36,697
{\an8}‎Quite a few friends of mine have had
‎to drop out from work because of stress.

306
00:18:36,698 --> 00:18:38,450
‎From putting up with so much all the time.

307
00:18:39,243 --> 00:18:42,371
‎They just snap all of a sudden.
‎They crash and burn.

308
00:18:42,996 --> 00:18:44,581
{\an8}‎I don't want that happening to you.

309
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,127
‎I'm still a long way
‎from entering the workforce.

310
00:18:49,253 --> 00:18:50,254
{\an8}‎That's true.

311
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:55,509
‎Still, us grown-ups do need
‎to be able to read the room.

312
00:18:56,218 --> 00:18:58,469
‎But then,
‎when you've got a large group of people,

313
00:18:58,470 --> 00:19:01,849
‎not everyone's going to have
‎the same opinion.

314
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:03,892
‎And do you know why?

315
00:19:04,726 --> 00:19:06,811
‎Because people like me exist.

316
00:19:06,812 --> 00:19:08,730
{\an8}‎CAN'T STAND THE STATUS QUO
‎A REBEL AT HEART

317
00:19:10,315 --> 00:19:12,733
‎Are you sure you're not
‎out of place at the shop?

318
00:19:12,734 --> 00:19:13,735
‎Don't be rude.

319
00:19:14,653 --> 00:19:17,488
{\an8}‎We all have likes and dislikes
‎and ideas about right and wrong,

320
00:19:17,489 --> 00:19:21,075
{\an8}‎so you need to have your own beliefs
‎and your own sense of self.

321
00:19:21,076 --> 00:19:24,328
‎And you need to know what they are.

322
00:19:24,329 --> 00:19:27,832
‎-I do?
‎-Yeah, and why you feel that way.

323
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:31,920
{\an8}‎You'll never reconcile with others
‎if you can't reconcile with yourself.

324
00:19:34,131 --> 00:19:35,132
{\an8}‎Kaito.

325
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:37,925
‎What happened to you after you left?

326
00:19:37,926 --> 00:19:40,179
‎Enough to have made me mellow out.

327
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:43,724
328
‎Keep on truckin', okay?

328
00:19:44,266 --> 00:19:46,852
‎Though I guess you don't say that
‎to someone who's not feeling well.

329
00:19:47,936 --> 00:19:49,145
‎Kaito.

330
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:50,355
‎Come back soon, okay?

331
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:52,106
‎Will do.

332
00:19:52,107 --> 00:19:54,401
‎I need to sneak in again
‎to return the seal.

333
00:19:55,068 --> 00:19:57,029
‎I don't mean it like that.

334
00:19:59,948 --> 00:20:02,242
<i>‎Do I do the things I do</i>

335
00:20:02,868 --> 00:20:05,287
<i>‎because I don't want
‎to end up like my brother?</i>

336
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,415
<i>‎No.</i>

337
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:13,170
<i>‎I never understood why
‎everyone hated him so much.</i>

338
00:20:13,879 --> 00:20:15,672
<i>‎I just felt scared.</i>

339
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:20,593
<i>‎Even those times I felt uncomfortable
‎when trying to go with the flow,</i>

340
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:24,430
<i>‎it wasn't about wanting to rebel
‎or to find justice for people</i>

341
00:20:24,431 --> 00:20:27,184
<i>‎when they were mislabeled
‎or succumbing to peer pressure.</i>

342
00:20:28,018 --> 00:20:31,188
<i>‎I just didn't understand
‎why they hated people so much.</i>

343
00:20:31,855 --> 00:20:34,774
<i>‎Some people point,
‎and some people get pointed at.</i>

344
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:36,610
<i>‎Right now, I'm not being pointed at.</i>

345
00:20:37,319 --> 00:20:40,404
<i>‎But the line that gets drawn
‎can change at any moment.</i>

346
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:45,452
<i>‎I found it hard to believe that all that
‎malice could be aimed at just one person.</i>

347
00:20:46,161 --> 00:20:51,123
<i>‎I felt that malice could be aimed at me
‎if I ever made a mistake someday.</i>

348
00:20:51,124 --> 00:20:54,670
‎You're a good kid, Minato.
‎Unlike your brother.

349
00:20:55,212 --> 00:20:58,715
<i>‎What if I were different?</i>

350
00:21:00,050 --> 00:21:01,509
<i>‎Kaito.</i>

351
00:21:01,510 --> 00:21:04,263
<i>‎I'm not as kind as you think I am.</i>

352
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:07,349
<i>‎I don't take care of others
‎for their sake.</i>

353
00:21:07,891 --> 00:21:09,518
<i>‎I'm not kind to people for their sake.</i>

354
00:21:10,310 --> 00:21:14,648
<i>‎I keep the peace
‎because I can't stand the tension.</i>

355
00:21:15,315 --> 00:21:17,817
<i>‎I reach out to others,</i>

356
00:21:17,818 --> 00:21:22,239
<i>‎because I'm scared if it were me,
‎nobody would be there to help me.</i>

357
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:25,659
<i>‎I can't bring myself to reject someone,</i>

358
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:30,497
<i>‎because I can't help but imagine
‎what it would be like in their shoes.</i>

359
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:34,042
<i>‎I'm not kind at all.</i>

360
00:21:35,043 --> 00:21:38,922
<i>‎I'm just weak and afraid of being alone.</i>

361
00:21:40,090 --> 00:21:44,845
<i>‎I've never been able to trust anyone
‎enough to fully open my heart to them.</i>

362
00:21:45,595 --> 00:21:49,766
<i>‎Not my family, not my friends, not anyone.</i>

363
00:21:50,642 --> 00:21:53,811
‎You only do it so people look to you.

364
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:55,856
‎You want them to depend on you.

365
00:21:57,441 --> 00:21:58,859
<i>‎Why do I remember that now?</i>

366
00:21:59,651 --> 00:22:03,238
<i>‎I thought I knew what she meant,
‎but now I actually feel it.</i>

367
00:22:04,823 --> 00:22:07,075
<i>‎I can't keep going like this.</i>

368
00:22:07,909 --> 00:22:11,038
<i>‎I act like I'm opening up,
‎but really, I can't.</i>

369
00:22:11,580 --> 00:22:13,206
<i>‎I'm hurting Momoka.</i>

370
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:17,252
<i>‎I'm just using people for my own purposes.</i>

371
00:22:18,754 --> 00:22:20,172
<i>‎I can't...</i>

372
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:23,091
<i>‎keep going out with her like this.</i>

373
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:55,934
‎Subtitle translation by: Rychelle Brittain

